{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>״I will not give, etc., even a foot-breadth,״ etc.</b> The meaning is: I am not giving you permission to pass through their land so that you would be able to coerce them regarding it; but if the children of Esau willingly allow them to pass through their land, HaShem does not forbid them the matter. Therefore they sent messengers with words of brotherhood and appeasement, in case they might wish to grant them a foot-breadth to pass through their land."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:26.106429906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}